Greek text: L. C. L. Brenton's Greek text (The Septuagint Version of the Old Testament, with an English Translation, 1851;
  Vaticanus-based), eBible.org "grcbrent", public domain. The text is shown as eBible prints it; only punctuation is removed from the tappable words.
English: L. C. L. Brenton's translation (1851), eBible.org eng-Brenton, public domain. It is paired with the Greek above verse by verse,
  by the same reference. Where a clause clearly translates the neighbouring Greek verse, it is moved there automatically
  (build/tools/resegment.py); such verses are marked with ↕ in the app.
LXX2012 (shown only as an "alternate rendering" line in the word pop-up for the few verses on a reviewed allowlist; build/tools/lxx2012_allow.py): LXX2012: Septuagint in American English (2012), Michael Paul Johnson; updates dedicated to the public domain; eBible.org eng-lxx2012.

New Testament Greek text, dictionary forms, Strong's numbers, grammar and glosses: STEPBible.org TAGNT (Translators Amalgamated Greek NT),
  "Data created by www.STEPBible.org based on work at Tyndale House Cambridge (CC BY 4.0)", https://github.com/STEPBible/STEPBible-Data.
  Credit: "STEP Bible" linked to www.STEPBible.org. Only words TAGNT marks as present in NA28 are used (137,919 words).
  Changes made (recorded here as the STEP licence page asks): punctuation removed from tappable words; Robinson grammar codes converted to
  this site's codes (build/tools/build_nt.py); crasis words tagged with the grammar of their last part; TAGNT glosses used where Dodson has no entry.
New Testament English: World English Bible (eBible.org eng-web, 2020 stable text), public domain; "World English Bible" is a trademark of eBible.org.
  Shown unchanged.

Dictionary forms (lemmas) and grammar tags: made automatically for this site. Forms Morpheus does not know are retried once
  with a regular spelling change (e.g. -οσαν to -ον; build/tools/prep_variants.py). The tags are the site's own output, not copied from a tagged text.
  - Morpheus morphological analyser (Perseus Project; perseids-tools/morpheus), Mozilla Public License 2.0. It was run on the build computer.
    Its analyses are used. Morpheus itself (code and stem library) is not included in the site.
  - STEPBible.org TAGNT (Translators Amalgamated Greek NT, Tyndale House, Cambridge), CC BY 4.0: NT word forms with their dictionary
    forms, used to choose between Morpheus analyses and for forms that Morpheus does not know.
  - STEPBible.org TBESG and TFLSJ headwords (CC BY 4.0) and Dodson headwords (public domain / CC0): used to spell dictionary forms and to
    match some names.
Dictionaries: STEPBible.org TBESG and TFLSJ (LSJ), Tyndale House, Cambridge, CC BY 4.0. The TBESG brief gloss is used as
  a plain meaning (label "STEP Bible") where Dodson has no entry.
Plain meanings: Dodson Greek-English Lexicon of the New Testament (Jeffrey Dodson; Ulrik Sandborg-Petersen conversion;
  github.com/biblicalhumanities/Dodson-Greek-Lexicon), public domain / CC0 1.0.
"Also in the NT" references: STEPBible TAGNT, CC BY 4.0. Words in the NA28 text, matched by dictionary form; only verse references and counts are stored.
Changes made to the dictionary text: spacing tidied; a leading "I"/"to" on verbs and "a/an/the" on nouns removed; Dodson's "am ..." written
  as "be ..."; STEP Bible's "base: specific" glosses reduced to the base; Dodson glosses with more than 3 senses or over 40 characters
  shortened to at most 3 of their own senses (full gloss under More); 19 headlines hand-written (build/tools/gloss_hand_plain.tsv, labelled
  "hand-written" on the card, original wording kept under More).
Brenton's wording (likely match): automatic word alignment built here from the Brenton Greek and Brenton English verse pairs only.
Font: Gentium Plus, SIL International, SIL Open Font License 1.1 (fonts/OFL.txt).

SEPARATE CC BY-SA 4.0 LAYERS (ShareAlike applies to these files only):
- Wiktionary contributors, via kaikki.org Wiktextract (Tatu Ylonen), CC BY-SA 4.0:
  - data/etym/ : etymologies and derived words;
  - data/wk/   : links from about 1,170 word forms (0.2% of words) to their dictionary form, for forms the sources above do not cover.
    The app applies these links when it shows a chapter. The card says "from Wiktionary, CC BY-SA 4.0" on these words.

Not used in this build: Rahlfs 1935, CCAT/CATSS (University of Pennsylvania) morphology or lexicon, eliranwong/LXX-Rahlfs-1935, the Open
Scriptures LXX lexeme data, James Tauber's corrections of the CCAT tags, SBLGNT, MorphGNT or Robinson-Pierpont (the NT-quotation notes were removed,
because they described the Rahlfs wording). Latin: no PROIEL data (CC BY-NC-SA), no LemLat, no LASLA data are shipped or read by the build.

TBESG definition sources, as marked in TBESG itself: (AS) Abbott-Smith, Manual Greek Lexicon of the NT (corrected by Tyndale House);
  (ML) edited Middle Liddell entries where Abbott-Smith has none; unmarked = TBESG brief gloss. The card's tab is named after that source.
  In this build: 5,311 entries Abbott-Smith, 2,115 Middle Liddell, 2,070 brief gloss only (12 of these NT entries look like Abbott-Smith text with the marker missing).
NT headword grouping: some TAGNT dictionary forms are shown under the usual dictionary headword (e.g. εἶπον under λέγω, aorist εἶδον
  under ὁράω, perfect οἶδα under οἶδα); the list is build/tools/nt_lemmas.py. Each word keeps TAGNT's form and grammar tag.

LATIN LAYER (Latin, Latin + English and Latin + Greek modes; Latin line in the Greek word card)
Latin text: Clementine Vulgate (1592/1598), eBible.org "latVUC", public domain. Vulgate spelling is kept; search is normalised (accents, ae/oe, j/i, v/u).
English: Douay-Rheims Bible, 1899 American edition, eBible.org "engDRA", public domain. Spacing before punctuation tidied.
Vulgate appendix (3 Esdras, 4 Esdras, Prayer of Manasseh): Hetzenauer, Biblia Sacra Vulgatae Editionis (1914), public domain. NOT INCLUDED in this build:
  the transcription made from page scans is not yet proofread and has verses missing, so the app shows a note instead of the text.
Latin dictionary forms and grammar: tagged automatically for this site with LatinCy (Patrick J. Burns; la_core_web_lg 3.9.8; MIT License), run on the
  build computer and not included in the app. Caveat on provenance: the LatinCy models are MIT-licensed, but they were trained on Universal Dependencies
  Latin treebanks and LASLA material, some of which carry NonCommercial or other restrictive terms. Only the tagger's output (dictionary forms and
  grammar codes) is used here, not any training data. Each form is checked against Whitaker's Words; a form is shown only when both agree (otherwise
  the word is shown without a dictionary form).
  - Whitaker's Words (William A. Whitaker, 1936-2010): "Permission is hereby freely given for any and all use of program and data." Used on the build computer.
Latin meanings: Lewis & Short, A Latin Dictionary (1879), digitised by the Perseus Digital Library (Tufts University), CC BY-SA 4.0,
  https://github.com/PerseusDL/lexica (lat.ls.perseus-eng1/eng2.xml), http://www.perseus.tufts.edu/. SEPARATE CC BY-SA 4.0 LAYER: data/ls/.
  Changes made: one short meaning per headword. Only hand-checked short meanings (build/tools/latin_gloss_hand.tsv, written for this site from
  Lewis & Short and labelled "hand-checked") are shown; automatic extracts are not shown until reviewed.
Greek-Latin word matches and verse pairing (data/vp/, data/vulmap.json): made for this site from the texts above by an open statistical method
  (build/tools/build_latin.py); only confident matches are shown. CC BY-SA 4.0 as original content of this project.
